</math>, <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math>, and <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math> are constants, <math alttext="left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is the center of the circle and the positive value of <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math> is the radius of the circle. In the given equation, <math alttext="h equals 13"><mrow>
<mi>h</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>13</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="r squared equals 64"><mrow>
<msup>
<mi>r</mi>
<mn>2</mn>
</msup>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>64</mn>
</mrow>
