    ($SATQ$aef4fd8a$SATQ$, $SATQ$d1c64540-1ef9-4449-9ccf-d158b23af654$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The length of each side of a square is <math alttext="94"><mn>94</mn></math> centimeters (cm). Which expression gives the area, in <math alttext="c m squared"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of the square?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"9eba2c8a-bad2-4708-9289-4dca6ce91a32","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2 dot 94\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>94</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"5cbdc099-5b25-4e18-bc15-a6b807a4a6ba","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2 dot 94 dot 94\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>94</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>94</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"d7028cb1-8905-46d5-aa1c-8f6e9b889b1c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4 dot 94\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>94</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"313f2015-afa0-4676-a9e6-a2ba0780b135","content":"<p><math alttext=\"94 dot 94\"><mn>94</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>94</mn></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["313f2015-afa0-4676-a9e6-a2ba0780b135"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. The area of a square is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="s squared"><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="s"><mi>s</mi></math> is the length of each side of the square. It's given that the length of each side of a square is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="94 cm"><mn>94</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>. It follows that the area, in&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="cm Superscript 2"><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of the square is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 94 right parenthesis 