\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554988,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"b4767bef","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":1,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1743430554988,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"f06ed67a-28a2-4bfe-9834-47786c3571e8","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"87f95af8-5ad5-4492-b535-c8ada8307545","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The lengths of two sides of a triangle are <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> centimeters and <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> centimeters. If the perimeter of the triangle is <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math> centimeters, what is the length, in centimeters, of the third side of this triangle?</p>","keys":["ebf374ac-c5b3-4685-9663-a2bdd4de2800"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"f2e3d00e-84be-4e9d-9462-dc3f97b32d99","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"ebf374ac-c5b3-4685-9663-a2bdd4de2800","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1d2d467d-1dc8-4584-b84b-1fa17b8781da","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4301d205-24ed-42fa-9d74-69137f06dce1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The perimeter of a triangle is the sum of the lengths of all three of its sides. It's given that the lengths of two sides of a triangle are <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> centimeters and <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> centimeters. Let <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> represent the length, in centimeters, of the third side of this triangle. The sum of the lengths