    ($SATQ$b8a225ff$SATQ$, $SATQ$a8b375f5-371f-458f-bca7-e5b78b360f11$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$3446b387-f8c0-41f5-ba9a-6a1607955d8c$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Circles$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Circle A in the <em>xy</em>-plane has the equation <math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 5 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 5 right parenthesis squared equals 4"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<msup>
			<mfenced>
				<mrow>
					<mi>x</mi>
					<mo>+</mo>
					<mn>5</mn>
				</mrow>
			</mfenced>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<msup>
			<mfenced>
				<mrow>
					<mi>y</mi>
					<mo>-</mo>
					<mn>5</mn>
				</mrow>
			</mfenced>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Circle B has the same center as circle A. The radius of circle B is two times the radius of circle A. The equation defining circle B in the <em>xy</em>-plane is <math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 5 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 5 right parenthesis squared equals k"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<msup>
			<mfenced>
				<mrow>
