    ($SATQ$ba8ca563$SATQ$, $SATQ$31c28a2a-1001-4c2c-b27f-aa2b2380c77d$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$c833f51c-8b19-420f-b804-24c5528a6b92$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A cube has a volume of <math alttext="474,552"><mn>474,552</mn>
</math> cubic units. What is the surface area, in square units, of the cube?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["36504"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["36504"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="36,504"><mn>36,504</mn>
</math>. The volume of a cube can be found using the formula <math alttext="upper V equals s cubed"><mrow>
	<mi>V</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<msup>
		<mi>s</mi>
		<mn>3</mn>
	</msup>
</mrow>
</math>, where <math alttext="s"><mi>s</mi>
</math> represents the edge length of a cube. It&rsquo;s given that this cube has a volume of <math alttext="474,552"><mn>474,552</mn>
</math> cubic units. Substituting <math alttext="474,552"><mn>474,552</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="upper V"><mi>V</mi>
</math> in <math alttext="upper V equals s cubed"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> yields <math alttext="474,552 equals s cubed"><mrow>
	<mn>474,552</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<msup>
		<mi>s</mi>
		<mn>3</mn>
	</msup>
</mrow>
</math>. Taking the cube root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="78 equals s"><mn>78</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></math>. Thus, the edge length of the cube is <math alttext="78"><mn>78</mn>
</math> units. Since each face of a cube is a square, it follows that each face has an edge length of <math alttext="78"><mn>78</mn>
</math> units. The area of a square can be found using the formula <math alttext="upper A equals s squared"><mrow>
	<mi>A</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<msup>
		<mi>s</mi>
		<mn>2</mn>
	</msup>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="78"><mn>78</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="s"><mi>s</mi>
</math> in this formula yields <math alttext="upper A equals 78 squared"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>78</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext="upper A equals 6,084"><mrow>
	<mi>A</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>6,084</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the area of one face of this cube is <math alttext="6,084"><mn>6,084</mn>
</math> square units. Since a cube has <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> faces, the surface area, in square units, of this cube is <math alttext="6 left parenthesis 6,084 right parenthesis"><mn>6</mn><mfenced><mn>6,084</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="36,504"><mn>36,504</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ba8ca563","external_id":"31c28a2a-1001-4c2c-b27f-aa2b2380c77d","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"c833f51c-8b19-420f-b804-24c5528a6b92","uId":"4785f6f3-cb7a-4e93-a8ef-f8f2082d46e1","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A cube has a volume of <math alttext=\"474,552\"><mn>474,552</mn>\n</math> cubic units. What is the surface area, in square units, of the cube?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["36504"],"correct_answer":["36504"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"36,504\"><mn>36,504</mn>\n</math>. The volume of a cube can be found using the formula <math alttext=\"upper V equals s cubed\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>V</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>s</mi>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math> represents the edge length of a cube. It&rsquo;s given that this cube has a volume of <math alttext=\"474,552\"><mn>474,552</mn>\n</math> cubic units. Substituting <math alttext=\"474,552\"><mn>474,552</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi>\n</math> in <math alttext=\"upper V equals s cubed\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"474,552 equals s cubed\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>474,552</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>s</mi>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Taking the cube root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"78 equals s\"><mn>78</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></math>. Thus, the edge length of the cube is <math alttext=\"78\"><mn>78</mn>\n</math> units. Since each face of a cube is a square, it follows that each face has an edge length of <math alttext=\"78\"><mn>78</mn>\n</math> units. The area of a square can be found using the formula <math alttext=\"upper A equals s squared\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>s</mi>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"78\"><mn>78</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math> in this formula yields <math alttext=\"upper A equals 78 squared\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>78</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"upper A equals 6,084\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>6,084</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the area of one face of this cube is <math alttext=\"6,084\"><mn>6,084</mn>\n</math> square units. Since a cube has <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> faces, the surface area, in square units, of this cube is <math alttext=\"6 left parenthesis 6,084 right parenthesis\"><mn>6</mn><mfenced><mn>6,084</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"36,504\"><mn>36,504</mn>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959836,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"ba8ca563","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1691007959836,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":null,"external_id":"31c28a2a-1001-4c2c-b27f-aa2b2380c77d","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"4785f6f3-cb7a-4e93-a8ef-f8f2082d46e1","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["36504"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"36,504\"><mn>36,504</mn>\n</math>. The volume of a cube can be found using the formula <math alttext=\"upper V equals s cubed\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>V</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>s</mi>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math> represents the edge length of a cube. It&rsquo;s given that this cube has a volume of <math alttext=\"474,552\"><mn>474,552</mn>\n</math> cubic units. Substituting <math alttext=\"474,552\"><mn>474,552</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi>\n</math> in <math alttext=\"upper V equals s cubed\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"474,552 equals s cubed\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>474,552</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>s</mi>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Taking the cube root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"78 equals s\"><mn>78</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></math>. Thus, the edge length of the cube is <math alttext=\"78\"><mn>78</mn>\n</math> units. Since each face of a cube is a square, it follows that each face has an edge length of <math alttext=\"78\"><mn>78</mn>\n</math> units. The area of a square can be found using the formula <math alttext=\"upper A equals s squared\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>s</mi>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"78\"><mn>78</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math> in this formula yields <math alttext=\"upper A equals 78 squared\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>78</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"upper A equals 6,084\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>6,084</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the area of one face of this cube is <math alttext=\"6,084\"><mn>6,084</mn>\n</math> square units. Since a cube has <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> faces, the surface area, in square units, of this cube is <math alttext=\"6 left parenthesis 6,084 right parenthesis\"><mn>6</mn><mfenced><mn>6,084</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"36,504\"><mn>36,504</mn>\n</math>.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A cube has a volume of <math alttext=\"474,552\"><mn>474,552</mn>\n</math> cubic units. What is the surface area, in square units, of the cube?</p>","externalid":"31c28a2a-1001-4c2c-b27f