454.058-.414,0-.798-.064-1.153-.194-.355-.129-.607-.251-.756-.368-.149-.116-.262-.226-.339-.329-2.571-3.269-3.992-5.09-4.263-5.465Z\" stroke-width=\"0\"></path><path d=\"m264.837,9.574c0-.387-.155-.765-.465-1.134-.311-.368-.686-.704-1.124-1.007-.439-.304-.882-.614-1.328-.931-.445-.316-.823-.688-1.134-1.114-.31-.426-.465-.878-.465-1.356,0-1.163.423-2.125,1.27-2.888.846-.762,1.87-1.144,3.071-1.144.336,0,.769.071,1.299.213.529.143.931.226,1.201.252-.09.711-.174,1.428-.252,2.151-.038.375-.067.594-.087.659-.02.065-.049.097-.087.097-.194,0-.343-.039-.446-.117-.025-.013-.038-.09-.038-.232,0-.607-.197-1.124-.592-1.55-.394-.426-.85-.64-1.366-.64-.736,0-1.33.223-1.782.668-.453.446-.679,1.005-.679,1.677,0,.685.316,1.279.949,1.783.246.194.666.498,1.26.911.595.414,1.024.73,1.289.949.265.22.526.533.785.94.258.407.388.837.388,1.289,0,.4-.098.827-.291,1.279-.193.453-.472.882-.833,1.289-.362.407-.841.743-1.435,1.007-.595.265-1.247.397-1.957.397-.698,0-1.725-.155-3.082-.465.052-.827.078-1.35.078-1.57s-.007-.517-.02-.892c-.013-.375-.02-.575-.02-.601,0-.09.123-.136.368-.136.116,0,.239.052.368.155,0,.271.029.543.088.814.058.271.167.562.329.872.161.31.42.559.775.746.354.188.784.281,1.288.281.685,0,1.302-.236,1.852-.708.549-.471.823-1.121.823-1.948Z\" stroke-width=\"0\"></path><polygon points=\"78.286 46.919 78.286 97.515 10.825 97.515 78.286 46.919\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polygon><polygon points=\"255.458 17.525 255.458 97.888 148.179 97.888 255.458 17.525\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polygon><rect x=\"244.197\" y=\"86.632\" width=\"11.335\" height=\"11.335\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\".945\"></rect><rect x=\"67.065\" y=\"86.111\" width=\"11.335\" height=\"11.335\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\".945\"></rect></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for right triangles upper J upper K upper L and upper R upper S upper T\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>Right triangle upper J upper K upper L is labeled as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Angle upper L is a right angle.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Right triangle upper R upper S upper T is labeled as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Angle upper T is a right angle.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>A note indicates the figures are not drawn to scale.</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the figure shown, triangle <math alttext=\"upper J upper K upper L\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>J</mi>\n\t<mi>K</mi>\n\t<mi>L</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"upper J\"><mi>J</mi>\n</math> corresponds to <math alttext=\"upper R\"><mi>R</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi>\n</math> corresponds to <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math>. The length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper J upper K\"><mover><mrow><mi>J</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn>\n</math>, and the perimeter of triangle <math alttext=\"upper J upper K upper L\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>J</mi>\n\t<mi>K</mi>\n\t<mi>L</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>\n</math>. The length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper R upper S\"><mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"135\"><mn>135</mn>\n</math>. What is the perimeter of triangle <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"3e80dd3d-7559-46ed-b599-280dad9ea356","content":"<p><math alttext=\"324\"><mn>324</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e2ce07be-4bb1-43bf-9caa-fb6bf5e4ff0f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"540\"><mn>540</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1b8cd5c2-a60b-47ad-89c8-3c854e19419f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2,916\"><mn>2,916</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"96db3ea2-87a8-4a27-9455-3ac74bec9eb5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8,100\"><mn>8,100</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["3e80dd3d-7559-46ed-b599-280dad9ea356"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper J upper K upper L\"><mi>J</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi></math> is similar to triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper J\"><mi>J</mi></math> corresponds to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R\"><mi>R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi></math> corresponds to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi></math>. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper J upper K\"><mover><mrow><mi>J</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> corresponds to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper R upper S\"><mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>. If two triangles are similar, then the scale factor between their perimeters is equal to the scale factor between the lengths of their corresponding sides. It's given that the length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper J upper K\"><mover><mrow><mi>J</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn></math> and the length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper R upper S\"><mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"135\"><mn>135</mn></math>. Therefore, the scale factor from the length&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper J upper K\"><mover><mrow><mi>J</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> to the length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper R upper S\"><mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 135 Over 15 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>135</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the perimeter of triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper J upper K upper L\"><mi>J</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi></math> represent the perimeter of triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math>. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction p Over 36 EndFraction equals 9\"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn></math> yields&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p equals 324\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>324</mn></math>. Therefore, the perimeter of triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"324\"><mn>324</mn></mat