square. It's given that square S has side lengths of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c m\"><mi>cm</mi></math>. It follows that the area, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c m squared\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of square S is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 squared\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"16\"><mn>16</mn></math>. Therefore, the total area, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c m squared\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of triangle R and square S is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"80 plus 16\"><mn>80</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"96\"><mn>96</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"09ef21b2-86ef-4977-8eef-37b47c81624e","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1755117017715,"updateDate":1755117017715}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017715, 1755117017715),
    ($SATQ$bbaac300$SATQ$, $SATQ$924b44e4-dcc1-47ff-ad3e-564a5a1991ef$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Right triangles and trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Triangle <math alttext="upper A upper B upper C"><mrow>
	<mi>A</mi>
	<mi>B</mi>
	<mi>C</mi>
</mrow>
</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext="upper D upper E upper F"><mrow>
	<mi>D</mi>
	<mi>E</mi>
	<mi>F</mi>
</mrow>
</math>, where angle <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math> corresponds to angle <math alttext="upper D"><mi>D</mi>
</math>, and angles<em> </em><math alttext="upper C"><mi>C</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="upper F"><mi>F</mi>
</math> are right angles. If <math alttext="cosine upper B equals one twenty second"><mi>cos</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>22</mn></mfrac></math>, what is the value of <math alttext="cosine upper E"><mi>cos</mi><mi>E</mi></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1c7fbfee-c8a5-4d95-a6e1-4d59adc4385b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"one twenty second\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t<mn>22</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1475f26a-8a8c-49ee-8cfe-1b150f9d1327","content":"<p><math alttext=\"one twenty third\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t<mn>23</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"a0da14f0-eece-47f9-8f66-d35044c13671","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 21 Over 22 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>21</mn>\n\t<mn>22</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"be260b54-0215-4268-9e04-ab543813ebc6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 22 Over 23 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>22</mn>\n\t<mn>23</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["1c7fbfee-c8a5-4d95-a6e1-4d59adc4385b"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. The cosine of an acute angle in a right triangle is defined as the ratio of the length of the leg adjacent to that angle to the length of the hypotenuse. It's given that angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper C"><mi>C</mi></math> is a right angle in triangle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A upper B upper C"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> and that angle F is a right angle in triangle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper D upper E upper F"><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="cosine upper B"><mi>cos</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is equal to the ratio of the length of side <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper B upper C"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> to the length of side <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A upper B"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="cosine upper E"><mi>cos</mi><mi>E</mi></math> is equal to the ratio of the length of side <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper E upper F"><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi></math> to the length of side <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper D upper E"><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi></math>. It&rsquo;s also given that triangle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A upper B upper C"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is similar to triangle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper D upper E upper F"><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi></math>, where angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi></math> corresponds to angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper D"><mi>D</mi></math>. Since similar triangles have proportional side lengths, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction upper B upper C Over upper A upper B EndFraction equals StartFraction upper E upper F Over upper D upper E EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="cosine upper B"><mi>cos</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is equal to the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="cosine upper E"><mi>cos</mi><mi>E</mi></math>. Since <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="cosine upper B equals one twenty second"><mi>cos</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>22</mn></mfrac></math>, the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="cosine upper E"><mi>cos</mi><mi>E</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="one twenty second"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>22</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>
