, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine upper B\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is equal to the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine upper E\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>E</mi></math>. Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine upper B equals one twenty second\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>22</mn></mfrac></math>, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine upper E\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>E</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one twenty second\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>22</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect&nbsp;and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect&nbsp;and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","externalid":"924b44e4-dcc1-47ff-ad3e-564a5a1991ef","correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1755117017721,"updateDate":1755117017721}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017721, 1755117017721),
    ($SATQ$bcb66188$SATQ$, $SATQ$62bc2dfe-0a0c-45ec-a764-c5f84ddbce67$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$d20a75cb-b0e3-42e8-bf52-d342e850550f$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Right triangles and trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Triangle <math alttext="upper F upper G upper H"><mrow>
	<mi>F</mi>
	<mi>G</mi>
	<mi>H</mi>
</mrow>
</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext="upper J upper K upper L"><mrow>
	<mi>J</mi>
	<mi>K</mi>
	<mi>L</mi>
</mrow>
</math>, where angle <math alttext="upper F"><mi>F</mi>
</math> corresponds to angle <math alttext="upper J"><mi>J</mi>
</math> and angles <math alttext="upper G"><mi>G</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="upper K"><mi>K</mi>
</math> are right angles. If <math alttext="sine left parenthesis upper F right parenthesis equals StartFraction 308 Over 317 EndFraction"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>F</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>308</mn><mn>317</mn></mfrac></mrow></math>, what is the value of <math alttext="sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis"><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>)</mo></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ae00d44c-9ee5-4524-aac2-6d8f6118919a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 75 Over 317 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>75</mn>\n\t<mn>317</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"faeacd70-4539-4aad-b1db-67e1f2265bb9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 308 Over 317 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>308</mn>\n\t<mn>317</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"90e604c9-cf62-4f87-a7d5-f1867a3cd081","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 317 Over 308 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>317</mn>\n\t<mn>308</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9bb36dc4-0d54-42b3-87ca-fff4941ae2a0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 317 Over 75 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>317</mn>\n\t<mn>75</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["faeacd70-4539-4aad-b1db-67e1f2265bb9"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. If two triangles are similar, then their corresponding angles are congruent. It's given that right triangle <math alttext="upper F upper G upper H"><mrow>
	<mi>F</mi>
	<mi>G</mi>
	<mi>H</mi>
</mrow>
</math> is similar to right triangle <math alttext="upper J upper K upper L"><mrow>
	<mi>J</mi>
	<mi>K</mi>
	<mi>L</mi>
</mrow>
</math> and angle <math alttext="upper F"><mi>F</mi>
</math> corresponds to angle <math alttext="upper J"><mi>J</mi>
</math>. It follows that angle <math alttext="upper F"><mi>F</mi>
</math> is congruent to angle <math alttext="upper J"><mi>J</mi>
</math> and, therefore, the measure of angle <math alttext="upper F"><mi>F</mi>
</math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext="upper J"><mi>J</mi>
</math>. The sine ratios of angles of equal measure are equal. Since the measure of angle <math alttext="upper F"><mi>F</mi>
</math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext="upper J"><mi>J</mi>
</math>, <math alttext="sine left parenthesis upper F right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>F</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>. It's given that <math alttext="sine left parenthesis upper F right parenthesis equals StartFraction 308 Over 317 EndFraction"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>F</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>308</mn><mn>317</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, &nbsp;<math alttext="sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math> is <math alttext="StartFraction 308 Over 317 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>308</mn><mn>317</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext="cosine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>, not the value of <math alttext="sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the reciprocal of the value of <math alttext="sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>, not the value of <math alttext="sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the reciprocal of the value of <math alttext="cosine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>, not the value of <math alttext="sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"bcb66188","external_id":"62bc2dfe-0a0c-45ec-a764-c5f84ddbce67","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"d20a75cb-b0e3-42e8-bf52-d342e850550f","uId":"04a12a1c-1d2a-43ce-bc5f-609b428a4bb8","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.C.","skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Triangle <math alttext=\"upper F upper G upper H\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>F</mi>\n\t<mi>G</mi>\n\t<mi>H</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper J upper K upper L\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>J</mi>\n\t<mi>K</mi>\n\t<mi>L</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where angle <math alttext=\"upper F\"><mi>F</mi>\n</math> corresponds to angle <math alttext=\"upper J\"><mi>J</mi>\n</math> and angles <math alttext=\"upper G\"><mi>G</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi>\n</math> are right angles. If <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper F right parenthesis equals StartFraction 308 Over 317 EndFraction\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>F</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>308</mn><mn>317</mn></mfrac></mrow></math>, what is the value of <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>)</mo></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"ae00d44c-9ee5-4524-aac2-6d8f6118919a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 75 Over 317 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>75</mn>\n\t<mn>317</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"faeacd70-4539-4aad-b1db-67e1f2265bb9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 308 Over 317 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>308</mn>\n\t<mn>317</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"90e604c9-cf62-4f87-a7d5-f1867a3cd081","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 317 Over 308 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>317</mn>\n\t<mn>308</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9bb36dc4-0d54-42b3-87ca-fff4941ae2a0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 317 Over 75 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>317</mn>\n\t<mn>75</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["faeacd70-4539-4aad-b1db-67e1f2265bb9"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. If two triangles are similar, then their corresponding angles are congruent. It's given that right triangle <math alttext=\"upper F upper G upper H\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>F</mi>\n\t<mi>G</mi>\n\t<mi>H</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to right triangle <math alttext=\"upper J upper K upper L\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>J</mi>\n\t<mi>K</mi>\n\t<mi>L</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> and angle <math alttext=\"upper F\"><mi>F</mi>\n</math> corresponds to angle <math alttext=\"upper J\"><mi>J</mi>\n</math>. It follows that angle <math alttext=\"upper F\"><mi>F</mi>\n</math> is congruent to angle <math alttext=\"upper J\"><mi>J</mi>\n</math> and, therefore, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper F\"><mi>F</mi>\n</math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper J\"><mi>J</mi>\n</math>. The sine ratios of angles of equal measure are equal. Since the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper F\"><mi>F</mi>\n</math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper J\"><mi>J</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper F right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>F</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>. It's given that <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper F right parenthesis equals StartFraction 308 Over 317 EndFraction\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>F</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>308</mn><mn>317</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, &nbsp;<math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math> is <math alttext=\"StartFraction 308 Over 317 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>308</mn><mn>317</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>, not the value of <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the reciprocal of the value of <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>, not the value of <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the reciprocal of the value of <math alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>, not the value of <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959840,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"bcb66188","skill_cd":"S.C.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","createDate":1691007959840,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":null,"external_id":"62bc2dfe-0a0c-45ec-a764-c5f84ddbce67","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"04a12a1c-1d2a-43ce-bc5f-609b428a4bb8","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["faeacd70-4539-4aad-b1db-67e1f2265bb9"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. If two triangles are similar, then their corresponding angles are congruent. It's given that right triangle <math alttext=\"upper F upper G upper H\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>F</mi>\n\t<mi>G</mi>\n\t<mi>H</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to right triangle <math alttext=\"upper J upper K upper L\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>J</mi>\n\t<mi>K</mi>\n\t<mi>L</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> and angle <math alttext=\"upper F\"><mi>F</mi>\n</math> corresponds to angle <math alttext=\"upper J\"><mi>J</mi>\n</math>. It follows that angle <math alttext=\"upper F\"><mi>F</mi>\n</math> is congruent to angle <math alttext=\"upper J\"><mi>J</mi>\n</math> and, therefore, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper F\"><mi>F</mi>\n</math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper J\"><mi>J</mi>\n</math>. The sine ratios of angles of equal measure are equal. Since the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper F\"><mi>F</mi>\n</math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper J\"><mi>J</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper F right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>F</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>. It's given that <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper F right parenthesis equals StartFraction 308 Over 317 EndFraction\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>F</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>308</mn><mn>317</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, &nbsp;<math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math> is <math alttext=\"StartFraction 308 Over 317 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>308</mn><mn>317</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>, not the value of <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the reciprocal of the value of <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>, not the value of <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the reciprocal of the value of <math alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>, not the value of <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Triangle <math alttext=\"upper F upper G upper H\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>F</mi>\n\t<mi>G</mi>\n\t<mi>H</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper J upper K upper L\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>J</mi>\n\t<mi>K</mi>\n\t<mi>L</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where angle <math alttext=\"upper F\"><mi>F</mi>\n</math> corresponds to angle <math alttext=\"upper J\"><mi>J</mi>\n</math> and angles <math alttext=\"upper G\"><mi>G</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi>\n</math> are right angles. If <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper F right parenthesis equals StartFraction 308 Over 317 EndFraction\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>F</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>308</mn><mn>317</mn></mfrac></mrow></math>, what is the value of <math alttext=\"sine left parenthesis upper J right parenthesis\"><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>)</mo></math>?</p>","externalid":"62bc2dfe-0a0c-45ec-a764-c5f84ddbce67","templateid":"cec7c28f-c417-4bf5-a857-a441ed54e2d0","vaultid":"d20a75cb-b0e3-42e8-bf52-d342e850550f","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"ae00d44c-9ee5-4524-aac2-6d8f6118919a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 75 Over 317 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>75</mn>\n\t<mn>317</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"faeacd70-4539-4aad-b1db-67e1f2265bb9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 308 Over 317 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>308</mn>\n\t<mn>317</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"90e604c9-cf62-4f87-a7d5-f1867a3cd081","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 317 Over 308 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>317</mn>\n\t<mn>308</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9bb36dc4-0d54-42b3-87ca-fff4941ae2a0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 317 Over 75 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>317</mn>\n\t<mn>75</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1691007959840,"updateDate":1691007959840}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959840, 1691007959840),
