</div>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">In the figure above, <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_001_77d1d2d3.png" alt="R T equals, T U"></span></span>. What is the&nbsp;value&nbsp;of&nbsp;<span class="italic">x</span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p>72</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>66</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>64</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>58</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. Since <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_002_77d1d2d3.png" alt="the length of side R T equals the length of side T U"></span>, it follows that <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_003_6631348b.png" alt="triangle R T U"></span> is an isosceles triangle with base <span class="italic">RU</span>. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_004_599dc412.png" alt="angle T R U"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_005_d6be48c4.png" alt="angle T U R"></span> are the base angles of an isosceles triangle and are congruent. Let the measures of both <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_006_599dc412.png" alt="angle T R U"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_007_d6be48c4.png" alt="angle T U R"></span> be <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_008_7523c547.png" alt="t degrees"></span>. According to the triangle sum theorem, the sum of the measures of the three angles of a triangle is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_009_429202ed.png" alt="180 degrees"></span>. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_010_6735a3cf.png" alt="114 degrees plus 2 t degrees, equals 180 degrees"></span>, so <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_011_8888cd43.png" alt="t equals 33"></span>.<p>Note that <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_012_d6be48c4.png" alt="angle T U R"></span> is the same angle as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_013_b56a91c5.png" alt="angle S U V"></span>. Thus, the measure of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_014_b56a91c5.png" alt="angle S U V"></span> is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_015_185a8aec.png" alt="33 degrees"></span>. According to the triangle exterior angle theorem, an external angle of a triangle is equal to the sum of the opposite interior angles. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_016_2e99d9a6.png" alt="x degrees"></span> is equal to the sum of the measures of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_017_dda00680.png" alt="angle V S U"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_018_b56a91c5.png" alt="angle S U V"></span>; that is, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_019_c7b2088c.png" alt="31 degrees plus 33 degrees, equals 64 degrees"></span>. Thus, the value of <span class="italic">x</span> is 64.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the measure of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_020_1e4fc520.png" alt="angle S T R"></span>, but <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_021_1e4fc520.png" alt="angle S T R"></span> is not congruent to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_022_5d36f0b1.png" alt="angle S V R"></span>. Choices A and D are incorrect and may result from a calculation error.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 23, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"bd7f6e30","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"11114-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\">\n\t<div class=\"standalone_image \"><img src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_000_8173f371.png\" alt=\"The figure presents triangle R T U, with R U horizontal, and U to the right of R. A point V is on R U, such that V is closer to R than it is to U. Vertex T is above R U. The angle at T is labeled 114 degrees. Side U T is extended to point S, above vertex R, and line segment S V is drawn. The angle to the right of S V and below S T is labeled 31 degrees. The angle to the left of S V and above R V is labeled x degrees.\" width=\"154\" height=\"115\"></div>\n</div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the figure above, <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_001_77d1d2d3.png\" alt=\"R T equals, T U\"></span></span>. What is the&nbsp;value&nbsp;of&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\">x</span> ?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p>72</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>66</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>64</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>58</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. Since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_002_77d1d2d3.png\" alt=\"the length of side R T equals the length of side T U\"></span>, it follows that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_003_6631348b.png\" alt=\"triangle R T U\"></span> is an isosceles triangle with base <span class=\"italic\">RU</span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_004_599dc412.png\" alt=\"angle T R U\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_005_d6be48c4.png\" alt=\"angle T U R\"></span> are the base angles of an isosceles triangle and are congruent. Let the measures of both <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_006_599dc412.png\" alt=\"angle T R U\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_007_d6be48c4.png\" alt=\"angle T U R\"></span> be <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_008_7523c547.png\" alt=\"t degrees\"></span>. According to the triangle sum theorem, the sum of the measures of the three angles of a triangle is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_009_429202ed.png\" alt=\"180 degrees\"></span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_010_6735a3cf.png\" alt=\"114 degrees plus 2 t degrees, equals 180 degrees\"></span>, so <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_011_8888cd43.png\" alt=\"t equals 33\"></span>.<p>Note that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_012_d6be48c4.png\" alt=\"angle T U R\"></span> is the same angle as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_013_b56a91c5.png\" alt=\"angle S U V\"></span>. Thus, the measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_014_b56a91c5.png\" alt=\"angle S U V\"></span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_015_185a8aec.png\" alt=\"33 degrees\"></span>. According to the triangle exterior angle theorem, an external angle of a triangle is equal to the sum of the opposite interior angles. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_016_2e99d9a6.png\" alt=\"x degrees\"></span> is equal to the sum of the measures of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_017_dda00680.png\" alt=\"angle V S U\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_018_b56a91c5.png\" alt=\"angle S U V\"></span>; that is, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_019_c7b2088c.png\" alt=\"31 degrees plus 33 degrees, equals 64 degrees\"></span>. Thus, the value of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> is 64.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_020_1e4fc520.png\" alt=\"angle S T R\"></span>, but <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_021_1e4fc520.png\" alt=\"angle S T R\"></span> is not congruent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd7f6e30/img_022_5d36f0b1.png\" alt=\"angle S V R\"></span>. Choices A and D are incorrect and may result from a calculation error.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":23,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959638,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"bd7f6e30","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1691007959638,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"11114-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"705adb84-79f7-45c0-b607-6be2e786044d","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"11114-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\">\n\t<div class=\"standalone_image \"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents triangle R T U, with R U horizontal, and U to the right of R. A point V is on R U, such that V is closer to R than it is to U. Vertex T is above R U. The angle at T is labeled 114 degrees. Side U T is extended to point S, above vertex R, and line segment S V is drawn. The angle to the right of S V and below S T is labeled 31 degrees. The angle to the left of S V and above R V is labeled x degrees.\" width=\"154\" height=\"115\"></div>\n</div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the figure above, <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"R T equals, T U\"></span></span>. What is the&nbsp;value&nbsp;of&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\">x</span> ?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p>72</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p>66</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p>64</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p>58</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"c","rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. Since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of side R T equals the length of side T U\"></span>, it follows that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"triangle R T U\"></span> is an isosceles triangle with base <span class=\"italic\">RU</span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle T R U\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle T U R\"></span> are the base angles of an isosceles triangle and are congruent. Let the measures of both <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle T R U\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle T U R\"></span> be <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"t degrees\"></span>. According to the triangle sum theorem, the sum of the measures of the three angles of a triangle is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"180 degrees\"></span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"114 degrees plus 2 t degrees, equals 180 degrees\"></span>, so <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"t equals 33\"></span>.<p>Note that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle T U R\"></span> is the same angle as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle S U V\"></span>. Thus, the measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle S U V\"></span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"33 degrees\"></span>. According to the triangle exterior angle theorem, an external angle of a triangle is equal to the sum of the opposite interior angles. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x degrees\"></span> is equal to the sum of the measures of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle V S U\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle S U V\"></span>; that is, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"31 degrees plus 33 degrees, equals 64 degrees\"></span>. Thus, the value of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> is 64.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle S T R\"></span>, but <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle S T R\"></span> is not congruent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle S V R\"></span>. Choices A and D are incorrect and may result from a calculation error.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959638,"updateDate":1691007959638}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959638, 1691007959638),
