$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Triangle <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_001_1f062fee.png" alt="A, B C"></span></span> above is a right triangle, and <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_002_f9eb4e12.png" alt="the sine of B, equals 5 over 13"></span></span>. What is the length of side <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_003_db819a7e.png" alt="B C"></span></span>?</p>
$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["24"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is 24. The sine of an acute angle in a right triangle is equal to the ratio of the length of the side opposite the angle to the length of the hypotenuse. In the triangle shown, the sine of angle <span class="italic">B</span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_004_5bfdac8e.png" alt="sine of B"></span>, is equal to the ratio of the length of side <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_005_80840f01.png" alt="A, C"></span> to the length of side <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_006_2dd66764.png" alt="A, B"></span><span class="italic">.</span> It&rsquo;s given that the length of side <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_007_2dd66764.png" alt="A, B"></span> is 26 and that <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_008_f9eb4e12.png" alt="sine of B equals, 5 over 13"></span>. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_009_0eae0690.png" alt="the fraction 5 over 13, equals, the fraction A, B over 26"></span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 26 yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_010_f1f71811.png" alt="A, C equals 10"></span>.<p>By the Pythagorean Theorem, the relationship between the lengths of the sides of triangle <span class="italic">ABC</span> is as follows: <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_011_f434bc1e.png" alt="26 squared equals, 10 squared, plus B C squared"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_012_9cef1f30.png" alt="676 equals, 100 plus B C squared"></span>. Subtracting 100 from both sides of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_013_9cef1f30.png" alt="676 equals, 100 plus B C squared"></span> yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_014_290ec999.png" alt="576 equals, B C squared"></span>. Taking the square root of both sides of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_015_290ec999.png" alt="576 equals, B C squared"></span> yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_016_d3065bc8.png" alt="24 equals B C"></span>.</p></p>
$SATQ$, true, 17, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$SPR$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"bd87bc09","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"029664-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.C.","skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \">\n          <img src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_000_ade2f571.png\" alt=\"The figure presents right triangle A, B C. Side A, C is horizontal, and vertex B is directly above vertex C. Angle C is a right angle. The length of side A, B is 26.\" width=\"58\" height=\"115\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Triangle <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_001_1f062fee.png\" alt=\"A, B C\"></span></span> above is a right triangle, and <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_002_f9eb4e12.png\" alt=\"the sine of B, equals 5 over 13\"></span></span>. What is the length of side <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_003_db819a7e.png\" alt=\"B C\"></span></span>?</p>\n","answerOptions":null,"keys":null,"correct_answer":["24"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 24. The sine of an acute angle in a right triangle is equal to the ratio of the length of the side opposite the angle to the length of the hypotenuse. In the triangle shown, the sine of angle <span class=\"italic\">B</span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_004_5bfdac8e.png\" alt=\"sine of B\"></span>, is equal to the ratio of the length of side <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_005_80840f01.png\" alt=\"A, C\"></span> to the length of side <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_006_2dd66764.png\" alt=\"A, B\"></span><span class=\"italic\">.</span> It&rsquo;s given that the length of side <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_007_2dd66764.png\" alt=\"A, B\"></span> is 26 and that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_008_f9eb4e12.png\" alt=\"sine of B equals, 5 over 13\"></span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_009_0eae0690.png\" alt=\"the fraction 5 over 13, equals, the fraction A, B over 26\"></span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 26 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_010_f1f71811.png\" alt=\"A, C equals 10\"></span>.<p>By the Pythagorean Theorem, the relationship between the lengths of the sides of triangle <span class=\"italic\">ABC</span> is as follows: <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_011_f434bc1e.png\" alt=\"26 squared equals, 10 squared, plus B C squared\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_012_9cef1f30.png\" alt=\"676 equals, 100 plus B C squared\"></span>. Subtracting 100 from both sides of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_013_9cef1f30.png\" alt=\"676 equals, 100 plus B C squared\"></span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_014_290ec999.png\" alt=\"576 equals, B C squared\"></span>. Taking the square root of both sides of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_015_290ec999.png\" alt=\"576 equals, B C squared\"></span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/bd87bc09/img_016_d3065bc8.png\" alt=\"24 equals B C\"></span>.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":17,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959626,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"bd87bc09","skill_cd":"S.C.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","createDate":1691007959626,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"029664-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"2e3f10e4-a193-467a-bbef-16e6fd5baabc","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"029664-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \">\n          <img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents right triangle A, B C. Side A, C is horizontal, and vertex B is directly above vertex C. Angle C is a right angle. The length of side A, B is 26.\" width=\"58\" height=\"115\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Triangle <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"A, B C\"></span></span> above is a right triangle, and <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the sine of B, equals 5 over 13\"></span></span>. What is the length of side <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"B C\"></span></span>?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 24. The sine of an acute angle in a right triangle is equal to the ratio of the length of the side opposite the angle to the length of the hypotenuse. In the triangle shown, the sine of angle <span class=\"italic\">B</span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"sine of B\"></span>, is equal to the ratio of the length of side <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"A, C\"></span> to the length of side <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"A, B\"></span><span class=\"italic\">.</span> It&rsquo;s given that the length of side <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"A, B\"></span> is 26 and that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"sine of B equals, 5 over 13\"></span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 5 over 13, equals, the fraction A, B over 26\"></span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 26 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"A, C equals 10\"></span>.<p>By the Pythagorean Theorem, the relationship between the lengths of the sides of triangle <span class=\"italic\">ABC</span> is as follows: <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"26 squared equals, 10 squared, plus B C squared\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"676 equals, 100 plus B C squared\"></span>. Subtracting 100 from both sides of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"676 equals, 100 plus B C squared\"></span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"576 equals, B C squared\"></span>. Taking the square root of both sides of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"576 equals, B C squared\"></span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"24 equals B C\"></span>.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959626,"updateDate":1691007959626,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959626, 1691007959626),
